First Author: Wang
Title: Comparison of Four Machine Learning Techniques for Prediction of Intensive Care Unit Length of Stay in Heart Transplantation Patients
Source number: 52  ￼

Very short summary: This single-center retrospective study compared several machine-learning methods for predicting prolonged ICU length of stay after heart transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) 365 heart-transplant recipients from Wuhan Union Hospital were included; (2) patients were split into 256 training and 109 test cases; (3) LASSO selected six key predictors, with ECMO use ranked most important by SHAP; (4) among the tested models, XGBoost performed best; and (5) the XGBoost model achieved AUC-ROC 0.88 with accuracy 0.87, sensitivity 0.98, specificity 0.51, PPV 0.86, and NPV 0.93 for predicting prolonged ICU stay. Figures 1–3 and Tables 1–2 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

